      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This article reviews the efficacy of medical and revascularization therapeutic interventions directed at the reduction or elimination of silent myocardial The review focuses on the use of standard anti-ischemic medications, including nitrates, calcium antagonists, and beta-blockers. In addition, data suggesting therapeutic benefit of antiplatelet agents are discussed. Finally, the results of studies evaluating the efficacy of revascularization with PTCA and coronary artery bypass graft surgery are reviewed."},
